 let you do it, but I guess since some of you goofballs are going to do it we have to carry the burden of at least making it work.\"}]\n4d:[\"$\",\"ol\",null,{\"className\":\"my-6 ml-6 list-decimal\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"font-medium\",\"children\":\"Nested lists are rarely a good idea.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"my-6 ml-6 list-disc\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":\"You might feel like you are being really \\\"organized\\\" or something but you are just creating a gross shape on the screen that is hard to read.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":\"Nested navigation in UIs is a bad idea too, keep things as flat as possible.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":\"Nesting tons of folders in your source code is also not helpful.\"}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"font-medium\",\"children\":\"Since we need to have more items, here's another one.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"my-6 ml-6 list-disc\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":\"I'm not sure if we'll bother styling more than two levels deep.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":\"Two is already too much, three is guaranteed to be a bad idea.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":\"If you nest four levels deep you belong in prison.\"}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"font-medium\",\"children\":\"Two items isn't really a list, three is good though.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"my-6 ml-6 list-disc\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":\"Again please don't nest lists if you want people to actually read your content.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":\"Nobody wants to look at this.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":\"I'm upset that we even have to bother styling this.\"}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n4e:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":[\"The most annoying thing about lists in Markdown is that \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted relative rounded-md px-[0.3rem] py-[0.1rem] font-mono outline-none\",\"children\":\"<li>\"}],\" elements aren't given a child \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted relative rounded-md px-[0.3rem] py-[0.1rem] font-mono outline-none\",\"children\":\"<p>\"}],\" tag unless there are multiple paragraphs in the list item. That means I have to worry about styling that annoying situation too.\"]}]\n4f:[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"my-6 ml-6 list-disc\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"font-medium\",\"children\":\"For example, here's another nested list.\"}]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":\"But this time with a second paragraph.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"my-6 ml-6 list-disc\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"These list items won't have \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted relative rounded-md px-[0.3rem] py-[0.1rem] font-mono outline-none\",\"children\":\"<p>\"}],\" tags\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":\"Because they are only one line each\"}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"className\":\"font-medium\",\"children\":\"But in this second top-level list item, they will.\"}]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":\"This is especially annoying because of the spacing on this paragraph.\"}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"className\":\"my-6 ml-6 list-disc\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":[\"As you can see here, because I've added a second line, this list item now has a \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted relative rounded-md px-[0.3rem] py-[0.1rem] font-mono outline-none\",\"children\":\"<p>\"}],\" tag.\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":\"This is the second line I'm talking about by the way.\"}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":\"Finally here's another list item so it's more like a list.\"}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-2\",\"children\":[\"\\n\",[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":\"A closing list item, but with no nested list, because why not?\"}],\"\\n\"]}],\"\\n\"]}]\n50:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":\"And finally a sentence to close off this section.\"}]\n51:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"there-are-other-elements-we-need-to-style\",\"className\":\"font-heading mt-12 scroll-m-28 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight first:mt-0 lg:mt-20 [&+p]:!mt-4\",\"children\":\"There are other elements we need to style\"}]\n52:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":[\"I almost forgot to mention links, like \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"font-medium underline underline-offset-4\",\"href\":\"https://tailwindcss.com\",\"children\":\"this link to the Tailwind CSS website\"}],\". We almost made them blue but that's so yesterday, so we went with dark gray, feels edgier.\"]}]\n53:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":\"We even included table styles, check it out:\"}]\n54:[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"my-6 w-full overflow-y-auto\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"table\",null,{\"className\":\"relative w-full overflow-hidden border-none text-sm\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"thead\",null,{\"children\":[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"className\":\"last:border-b-none m-0 border-b\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 text-left font-bold [&[align=center]]:text-center [&[align=right]]:text-right\",\"children\":\"Wrestler\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 text-left font-bold [&[align=center]]:text-center [&[align=right]]:text-right\",\"children\":\"Origin\"}],[\"$\",\"th\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 text-left font-bold [&[align=center]]:text-center [&[align=right]]:text-right\",\"children\":\"Finisher\"}]]}]}],[\"$\",\"tbody\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"className\":\"last:border-b-none m-0 border-b\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 text-left [&[align=center]]:text-center [&[align=right]]:text-right\",\"children\":\"Bret \\\"The Hitman\\\" Hart\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 text-left [&[align=center]]:text-center [&[align=right]]:text-right\",\"children\":\"Calgary, AB\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 text-left [&[align=center]]:text-center [&[align=right]]:text-right\",\"children\":\"Sharpshooter\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"className\":\"last:border-b-none m-0 border-b\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 text-left [&[align=center]]:text-center [&[align=right]]:text-right\",\"children\":\"Stone Cold Steve Austin\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 text-left [&[align=center]]:text-center [&[align=right]]:text-right\",\"children\":\"Austin, TX\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 text-left [&[align=center]]:text-center [&[align=right]]:text-right\",\"children\":\"Stone Cold Stunner\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"className\":\"last:border-b-none m-0 border-b\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 text-left [&[align=center]]:text-center [&[align=right]]:text-right\",\"children\":\"Randy Savage\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 text-left [&[align=center]]:text-center [&[align=right]]:text-right\",\"children\":\"Sarasota, FL\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 text-left [&[align=center]]:text-center [&[align=right]]:text-right\",\"children\":\"Elbow Drop\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"className\":\"last:border-b-none m-0 border-b\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 text-left [&[align=center]]:text-center [&[align=right]]:text-right\",\"children\":\"Vader\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 text-left [&[align=center]]:text-center [&[align=right]]:text-right\",\"children\":\"Boulder, CO\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 text-left [&[align=center]]:text-center [&[align=right]]:text-right\",\"children\":\"Vader Bomb\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"tr\",null,{\"className\":\"last:border-b-none m-0 border-b\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 text-left [&[align=center]]:text-center [&[align=right]]:text-right\",\"children\":\"Razor Ramon\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 text-left [&[align=center]]:text-center [&[align=right]]:text-right\",\"children\":\"Chuluota, FL\"}],[\"$\",\"td\",null,{\"className\":\"px-4 py-2 text-left [&[align=center]]:text-center [&[align=right]]:text-right\",\"children\":\"Razor's Edge\"}]]}]]}]]}]}]\n55:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":[\"We also need to make sure inline code looks good, like if I wanted to talk about \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted relative rounded-md px-[0.3rem] py-[0.1rem] font-mono outline-none\",\"children\":\"<span>\"}],\" elements or tell you the good news about \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted relative rounded-md px-[0.3rem] py-[0.1rem] font-mono outline-none\",\"children\":\"@tailwindcss/typography\"}],\".\"]}]\n56:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-heading mt-8 scroll-m-28 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight\",\"children\":[\"Sometimes I even use \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted relative rounded-md px-[0.3rem] py-[0.1rem] font-mono outline-none\",\"children\":\"code\"}],\" in headings\"]}]\n57:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":[\"Even though it's probably a bad idea, and historically I've had a hard time making it look good. This \",[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"\\\"wrap the code blocks in backticks\\\"\"}],\" trick works pretty well though really.\"]}]\n58:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":[\"Another thing I've done in the past is put a \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted relative rounded-md px-[0.3rem] py-[0.1rem] font-mono outline-none\",\"children\":\"code\"}],\" tag inside of a link, like if I wanted to tell you about the \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"font-medium underline underline-offset-4\",\"href\":\"https://github.com/tailwindcss/docs\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted relative rounded-md px-[0.3rem] py-[0.1rem] font-mono outline-none\",\"children\":\"tailwindcss/docs\"}]}],\" repository. I don't love that there is an underline below the backticks but it is absolutely not worth the madness it would require to avoid it.\"]}]\n59:[\"$\",\"h4\",null,{\"className\":\"font-heading mt-8 scroll-m-28 text-lg font-medium tracking-tight\",\"children\":[\"We haven't used an \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted relative rounded-md px-[0.3rem] py-[0.1rem] font-mono outline-none\",\"children\":\"h4\"}],\" yet\"]}]\n5a:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":[\"But now we have. Please don't use \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted relative rounded-md px-[0.3rem] py-[0.1rem] font-mono outline-none\",\"children\":\"h5\"}],\" or \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted relative rounded-md px-[0.3rem] py-[0.1rem] font-mono outline-none\",\"children\":\"h6\"}],\" in your content, Medium only supports two heading levels for a reason, you animals. I honestly considered using a \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted relative rounded-md px-[0.3rem] py-[0.1rem] font-mono outline-none\",\"children\":\"before\"}],\" pseudo-element to scream at you if you use an \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted relative rounded-md px-[0.3rem] py-[0.1rem] font-mono outline-none\",\"children\":\"h5\"}],\" or \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted relative rounded-md px-[0.3rem] py-[0.1rem] font-mono outline-none\",\"children\":\"h6\"}],\".\"]}]\n5b:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":[\"We don't style them at all out of the box because \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted relative rounded-md px-[0.3rem] py-[0.1rem] font-mono outline-none\",\"children\":\"h4\"}],\" elements are already so small that they are the same size as the body copy. What are we supposed to do with an \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted relative rounded-md px-[0.3rem] py-[0.1rem] font-mono outline-none\",\"children\":\"h5\"}],\", make it \",[\"$\",\"em\",null,{\"children\":\"smaller\"}],\" than the body copy? No thanks.\"]}]\n5c:[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"className\":\"font-heading mt-8 scroll-m-28 text-xl font-semibold tracking-tight\",\"children\":\"We still need to think about stacked headings though.\"}]\n5d:[\"$\",\"h4\",null,{\"className\":\"font-heading mt-8 scroll-m-28 text-lg font-medium tracking-tight\",\"children\":[\"Let's make sure we don't screw that up with \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted relative rounded-md px-[0.3rem] py-[0.1rem] font-mono outline-none\",\"children\":\"h4\"}],\" elements, either.\"]}]\n5e:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":\"Phew, with any luck we have styled the headings above this text and they look pretty good.\"}]\n5f:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":\"Let's add a closing paragraph here so things end with a decently sized block of text. I can't explain why I want things to end that way but I have to assume it's because I think things will look weird or unbalanced if there is a heading too close to the end of the document.\"}]\n60:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":\"What I've written here is probably long enough, but adding this final sentence can't hurt.\"}]\n61:[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"id\":\"github-flavored-markdown\",\"className\":\"font-heading mt-12 scroll-m-28 text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight first:mt-0 lg:mt-20 [&+p]:!mt-4\",\"children\":\"GitHub Flavored Markdown\"}]\n62:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":[\"I've also added support for GitHub Flavored Mardown using \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted relative rounded-md px-[0.3rem] py-[0.1rem] font-mono outline-none\",\"children\":\"remark-gfm\"}],\".\"]}]\n63:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":[\"With \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted relative rounded-md px-[0.3rem] py-[0.1rem] font-mono outline-none\",\"children\":\"remark-gfm\"}],\", we get a few extra features in our markdown. Example: autolink literals.\"]}]\n64:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":[\"A link like \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"font-medium underline underline-offset-4\",\"href\":\"http://www.example.com\",\"children\":\"www.example.com\"}],\" or \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"font-medium underline underline-offset-4\",\"href\":\"https://example.com\",\"children\":\"https://example.com\"}],\" would automatically be converted into an \",[\"$\",\"code\",null,{\"className\":\"bg-muted relative rounded-md px-[0.3rem] py-[0.1rem] font-mono outline-none\",\"children\":\"a\"}],\" tag.\"]}]\n65:[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"leading-relaxed [&:not(:first-child)]:mt-6\",\"children\":[\"This works for email links too: \",[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"className\":\"font-medium underline underline-offset-4\",\"href\":\"mailto:contact@example.com\",\"children\":\"contact@example.com\"}],\".\"]}]\n67:[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"data-line\":\"\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"style\":{\"--shiki-dark\":\"#E1E4E8\",\"--shiki-light\":\"#1F2328\"},\"children\":\"    series of rabies cases springing up around the country.\"}]}]\n68:[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"data-line\":\"\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"style\":{\"--shiki-dark\":\"#E1E4E8\",\"--shiki-light\":\"#1F2328\"},\"children\":\"  </\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"style\":{\"--shiki-dark\":\"#85E89D\",\"--shiki-light\":\"#116329\"},\"children\":\"p\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"style\":{\"--shiki-dark\":\"#E1E4E8\",\"--shiki-light\":\"#1F2328\"},\"children\":\">\"}]]}]\n69:[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"data-line\":\"\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"style\":{\"--shiki-dark\":\"#E1E4E8\",\"--shiki-light\":\"#1F2328\"},\"children\":\"</\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"style\":{\"--shiki-dark\":\"#85E89D\",\"--shiki-light\":\"#116329\"},\"children\":\"article\"}],[\"